From 0b3ebee3be93b42e937278a697361d76b07b3d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:59:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): persist Cmd-B parks for older drawn sessions
 [daveey]

The recent session store omits older rows still drawn by other sidebar
sources, so Cmd-B used local-only state that backend muted=false outranked.
Remember up to 1000 drawn rows with lineage-aware lookup and route writes
through their connection/profile. Retain acknowledged writes for ten minutes
until a refreshed row agrees; unacknowledged writes retain the ten-second TTL.

Keep the registry reset in a dependency-light module: importing the full
session-blocked store in global vitest setup preloads RPC modules before
per-file mocks, breaking existing write-through tests.

Proof: new tests failed on unchanged source before implementation (six
failures, sixteen controls passed); extra lineage case failed before its
lookup fix. All seven consumer suites now pass, 146 tests. Desktop tsc
passes with a 3GiB heap, eslint passes, and scripts/check --base origin/main
passes all 21 checks including health (zero blocking/advisory).
